  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of tigers and tiger prey in Thailands Western Forest Complex (WEFCOM) through law enforcement and education-Year 8</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to bring the tiger population back to its natural carrying capacity in the World Heritage Site, including Huai Kha Khaeng (HKK) and Thung Yai (TY) Wildlife Sanctuaries. The project will maintain the SMART (Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool) patrol system, provide continuous training and necessary equipment, to ensure a strong law enforcement staff to protect tigers, tiger-prey and other wildlife against poaching. Project will also build a conservation volunteer network at Huai Kha Khaeng Wildlife Sanctuary.</narrative>
  </description>
